I'm compiling this on my unix machine, using the Haskell Platform from wine.
    wine cabal install
basically works for me, except that the only way I've found to stop it trying
to use my locally installed mingw32 libraries in /usr/i386-mingw32/ is to
rename that directory while compiling. Yes.

Compiling the libraries in winlibs was an extremely painful process, which is
why I'm putting them in the tree so I don't lose them. Basically I did a
cross-compilation for each library, with
    CC="wine gcc" ./configure --host i386-mingw32
, and then when it started linking and building libraries using my unix
toolchain, I reran the commands with 'wine' prepended. Pain.
